  <div id="sutta">
  
    <h4 id="thag5.1" class="h1">Thag 5:1  Rājadatta</h4>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>I, a monk,</p>
              <p>gone to the charnel ground,</p>
              <p>saw a woman cast away,</p>
              <p class="v2">discarded</p>
              <p>there in the cemetery.</p>
              <p>Though some were disgusted,</p>
              <p>seeing her—dead, evil—</p>
              <p class="v6">lust</p>
              <p class="v2">appeared,</p>
              <p>as if I were blind</p>
              <p class="v2">to the oozings.</p>
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>In less time than it takes</p>
                <p>for rice to cook,</p>
                <p>I got out of that place.</p>
                <p>Mindful, alert, I</p>
                <p>sat down to one side.</p>
                <p>Then apt attention arose in me,</p>
                <p>the drawbacks appeared,</p>
                <p class="v2">disenchantment stood</p>
                <p class="v2">at an even keel:</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>With that, my heart was released.</p>
                <p>See the Dhamma’s true rightness!</p>
                <p>The three knowledges</p>
                <p>have been attained;</p>
                <p>the Awakened One’s bidding,</p>
                <p class="v4">done.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
            </div><!--end verse-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
